{"audit_run_id":"audit:880dfb5a0da64d0ca24d735623be2677","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":96,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Sixty commercial turkey poults of the same hatch and strain were reared to twelve weeks of age."},{"end_column":101,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"Feeding, stocking density, and ventilation were identical for all birds. The only difference between"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"the two groups was the floor bedding: 30 birds were reared on chopped straw and 30 birds on softwood"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"shavings. Each bird was measured individually at the end of the rearing period, so the bird is the"},{"end_column":53,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"unit of analysis and the two groups are independent."},{"end_column":102,"end_line":11,"start_column":1,"start_line":11,"text":"Six bird-level outcomes were declared before the trial began, in this order: live body weight, breast"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":12,"start_column":1,"start_line":12,"text":"yield, footpad dermatitis score, hock burn score, tibia ash content, and plasma corticosterone."},{"end_column":102,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"The analysis reads `turkey_bedding.csv`. One row is one bird, measured once at twelve weeks. The file"},{"end_column":56,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"has a header row and 60 data rows, with no blank cells."},{"end_column":27,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"| Column | What it holds |"},{"end_column":14,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"| --- | --- |"},{"end_column":63,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"| `bird_id` | Unique bird identifier, `T001` through `T060`. |"},{"end_column":86,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"| `bedding` | Bedding group: `chopped_straw` or `softwood_shavings`, 30 birds each. |"},{"end_column":71,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"| `body_weight_kg` | Live body weight at twelve weeks, in kilograms. |"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"| `breast_yield_pct` | Breast muscle yield as a percentage of carcass weight. |"},{"end_column":103,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"| `footpad_score` | Footpad dermatitis score, whole number 0 to 4; 0 is no lesion, 4 is most severe. |"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"| `hock_burn_score` | Hock burn score, whole number 0 to 2; 0 is no lesion, 2 is most severe. |"},{"end_column":71,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"| `tibia_ash_pct` | Tibia ash content, percent of dry defatted bone. |"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"| `plasma_cort_ng_per_ml` | Plasma corticosterone at slaughter, in nanograms per millilitre. |"},{"end_column":102,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"For each declared outcome in turn, the two bedding groups were compared with a two-sample t-test that"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"does not assume equal group variances (Welch's test). The script reports the mean of each group, the"},{"end_column":102,"end_line":34,"start_column":1,"start_line":34,"text":"difference between them (straw minus shavings), and the p-value. An outcome is declared significantly"},{"end_column":52,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"affected by bedding when its p-value is below 0.05."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":39,"start_column":1,"start_line":39,"text":"Group means, the straw-minus-shavings difference, and the p-value for each declared outcome, in the"},{"end_column":16,"end_line":40,"start_column":1,"start_line":40,"text":"declared order:"},{"end_column":84,"end_line":42,"start_column":1,"start_line":42,"text":"| Outcome | Chopped straw | Softwood shavings | Difference | p-value | Conclusion |"},{"end_column":38,"end_line":43,"start_column":1,"start_line":43,"text":"| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":44,"start_column":1,"start_line":44,"text":"| Live body weight (kg) | 12.60 | 13.40 | -0.80 | 0.0006 | Significantly affected by bedding |"},{"end_column":105,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"| Breast yield (% of carcass) | 27.10 | 27.15 | -0.05 | 0.8987 | Not significantly affected by bedding |"},{"end_column":103,"end_line":46,"start_column":1,"start_line":46,"text":"| Footpad dermatitis score (0-4) | 2.53 | 1.27 | +1.27 | 0.00003 | Significantly affected by bedding |"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":47,"start_column":1,"start_line":47,"text":"| Hock burn score (0-2) | 0.70 | 0.50 | +0.20 | 0.2844 | Not significantly affected by bedding |"},{"end_column":105,"end_line":48,"start_column":1,"start_line":48,"text":"| Tibia ash (% dry defatted bone) | 48.20 | 49.20 | -1.00 | 0.0462 | Significantly affected by bedding |"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":49,"start_column":1,"start_line":49,"text":"| Plasma corticosterone (ng/mL) | 3.60 | 2.40 | +1.20 | 0.0016 | Significantly affected by bedding |"},{"end_column":35,"end_line":51,"start_column":1,"start_line":51,"text":"Conclusion drawn for each outcome:"},{"end_column":103,"end_line":53,"start_column":1,"start_line":53,"text":"1. **Live body weight.** Birds on softwood shavings were 0.80 kg heavier at twelve weeks than birds on"},{"end_column":62,"end_line":54,"start_column":4,"start_line":54,"text":"chopped straw. Bedding significantly affected body weight."},{"end_column":104,"end_line":55,"start_column":1,"start_line":55,"text":"2. **Breast yield.** The two groups differed by 0.05 percentage points, which is a difference of almost"},{"end_column":63,"end_line":56,"start_column":4,"start_line":56,"text":"nothing. Bedding did not significantly affect breast yield."},{"end_column":103,"end_line":57,"start_column":1,"start_line":57,"text":"3. **Footpad dermatitis score.** Birds on chopped straw scored 1.27 points higher on the 0 to 4 scale,"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":58,"start_column":4,"start_line":58,"text":"the largest effect in the family. Bedding significantly affected footpad dermatitis."},{"end_column":102,"end_line":59,"start_column":1,"start_line":59,"text":"4. **Hock burn score.** Birds on chopped straw scored 0.20 points higher on the 0 to 2 scale, but the"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":60,"start_column":4,"start_line":60,"text":"groups overlapped too much for that gap to clear the threshold. Bedding did not significantly"},{"end_column":21,"end_line":61,"start_column":4,"start_line":61,"text":"affect hock burn."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":62,"start_column":1,"start_line":62,"text":"5. **Tibia ash.** Birds on softwood shavings had 1.00 percentage point more ash in the tibia. The"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":63,"start_column":4,"start_line":63,"text":"p-value of 0.0462 sits just under the threshold. Bedding significantly affected tibia ash."},{"end_column":104,"end_line":64,"start_column":1,"start_line":64,"text":"6. **Plasma corticosterone.** Birds on chopped straw had corticosterone 1.20 ng/mL higher at slaughter."},{"end_column":57,"end_line":65,"start_column":4,"start_line":65,"text":"Bedding significantly affected plasma corticosterone."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":69,"start_column":1,"start_line":69,"text":"The picture that comes out of these six comparisons favours softwood shavings. The clearest welfare"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":70,"start_column":1,"start_line":70,"text":"signal is footpad dermatitis: birds on chopped straw carried noticeably worse footpad lesions, and"},{"end_column":103,"end_line":71,"start_column":1,"start_line":71,"text":"footpad lesions are painful and limit how freely a bird moves. Plasma corticosterone, a stress hormone"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":72,"start_column":1,"start_line":72,"text":"measured in the blood at slaughter, was also higher in the straw group, which points the same way."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":73,"start_column":1,"start_line":73,"text":"Straw-reared birds were lighter at twelve weeks and had slightly less mineral in the tibia, so the"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":74,"start_column":1,"start_line":74,"text":"bone-strength and growth measures line up with the lesion and stress measures rather than cutting"},{"end_column":14,"end_line":75,"start_column":1,"start_line":75,"text":"against them."},{"end_column":104,"end_line":77,"start_column":1,"start_line":77,"text":"Two outcomes showed no significant effect. Breast yield was essentially identical, so the carcass value"},{"end_column":102,"end_line":78,"start_column":1,"start_line":78,"text":"of the bird did not depend on the bedding. Hock burn leaned the same direction as footpad dermatitis,"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":79,"start_column":1,"start_line":79,"text":"with straw birds scoring higher on average, but the difference in this flock was not large enough to"},{"end_column":6,"end_line":80,"start_column":1,"start_line":80,"text":"call."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":82,"start_column":1,"start_line":82,"text":"Taken together, the results support softwood shavings over chopped straw for growing turkeys on"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":83,"start_column":1,"start_line":83,"text":"welfare grounds, with the footpad result carrying the most weight because it measures a lesion the"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":84,"start_column":1,"start_line":84,"text":"bird lives with every day. These are single-flock results from birds reared under one set of housing"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":85,"start_column":1,"start_line":85,"text":"conditions, so confirming them in a second flock would strengthen the case before a producer changes"},{"end_column":9,"end_line":86,"start_column":1,"start_line":86,"text":"bedding."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:cf7ced0c316be28a9678","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:929b419775dfa6ef214a1930a77e600637a817195f5812f9d189cb7e9d7c8b9c","end_line":86,"locator":"report.md:1-86","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
